From e79e4e30e91c47ac248be791199ae8057f10cfc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Subrata Chatterjee <schatterjee@habana.ai>
Date: Mon, 12 Jul 2021 14:55:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SW-45031] preboot code restructure

For platforms like Greco, Gaudi2, code duplications
are there between different build types (e.g.
between greco_arc and greco_gnu_arc). If these duplications
are removed, then it code would be much cleaner and hence would
be easy to maintain.
In this context, preboot code is restructured. This is preparation
patch for that. Following  are few changes,
 - ARCHITECTURE specific duplicate code can be
   put into a 'common' subdir.
 - Also the application code is moved to a different
   'app' directory to differentiate it from rest of the code.
 - To avoid carrying the name 'arc_gnu' for future socs,
   existing 'arc_gnu' dir is renamed as 'arc' and 'arc' is renamed as
   'arc_elf32'. Build options are also being changed accordingly.

Following is the new dir strucutre,

├── app
│   ├── ext_rom
│   ├── ppboot
│   ├── preboot
│   └── recovery
├── arch
│   ├── gaudi
│   │   └── arm
│   ├── gaudi2
│   │   ├── arc
│   │   ├── arm
│   │   └── common
│   ├── goya
│   │   └── arm
│   └── greco
│       ├── arc
│       ├── arc_elf32
│       ├── arm
│       └── common
├── include
└── lib
    ├── common
    │   └── lzo
    └── preboot

Change-Id: I35e6dad7667622bce0da24080b71dc7231a601dd
Signed-off-by: Subrata Chatterjee <schatterjee@habana.ai>
---

